  "description": "Allowance usage (wire 6.5, spec 11.3 with specs/allowances.md): for every period limit the amount and count of counted entries in the period containing t (anchored) or with t < at + 60 s + L (rolling), the lifetime amount including the ledger's compacted totals, and how many entries are reserved, spent and released. An entry's own done spends, and its own failed releases unless its attempt's claim is now done (which spends); an entry without an outcome counts by its attempt's claim state (claims): open and unknown reserve, done spends, failed releases only when the attempt's owner wrote it (resolved_by_owner true), a failed another app wrote stays reserved until the user releases it, and an entry whose claim is gone spends. Candidates are checked against every limit; refused_by names the first limit that refuses. A totals.failed item counts like an entry's own failed, in the lifetime amount only: it adds its value while its attempt's claim is done, until the executor moves it into spent and count. Compaction keeps each compacted failed entry's attempt, obligation and value in totals.failed."
